endship.","A final label alone is weaker than a stated reason."],"teach2":["Compare an unsafe or unkind choice with a better one.","Change the choice or strategy, not only the words.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh place, game or situation that still uses the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked example as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original reasons and a short reflection.","Save work that shows the skill in a new situation."]},"subject":"Movement Skill and Performance","success_criteria":["I can use dance with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify skill and explain why it matters.","I can practise space independently on a new prompt.","I can notice control needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Dance skills practice uses locomotor/non-locomotor moves, levels and pathways with control and safe spacing. Supported choices follow the actual cues, rules and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Dance skills practice uses locomotor/non-locomotor moves, levels and pathways with control and safe spacing","A choice unrelated to safety, health or respect","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no reason"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about dance with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: travel-pathway-turn-balance sequence in personal space.\n\nTRY FIRST\nName two space-awareness rules for dance class.\n\nFEEDBACK\nKeep personal space; control stops — any two.","explain":"Dance skills practice uses locomotor/non-locomotor moves, levels and pathways with control and safe spacing.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make safe, healthy and respectful choices using clear cues 